1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:02,240
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:03,440
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:05,240
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:08,980
(Episode 16)

5
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:10,950
- Chief Cha.
- Ms. Joo.

6
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:18,160
What is Ko Eun Seol doing here?

7
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,530
We're personally acquainted,
so I was just curious what happened.

8
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:26,360
All right, you can go now.

9
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:28,800
Okay.

10
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:39,840
So, what brings you
to my office, Ms. Joo?

11
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:44,080
She seems like more
than just an acquaintance.

12
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:46,320
Pardon?

13
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:50,190
I saw how you defended her
at the awards ceremony.

14
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:53,690
For someone to step in
during a situation like that,

15
00:00:54,730 --> 00:00:56,460
you two must have been very close.

16
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:58,800
It's nothing like that.

17
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:03,940
Good, then.

18
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,970
What do you mean by "good?"

19
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:08,010
If there's nothing between you two,

20
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:10,510
you'll have no reason
to protect her.

21
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:12,180
That's what I meant.

22
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:15,250
There's no need to bring
a troublemaker into Cheongma.

23
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:16,920
Right?

24
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:19,780
I'm sure the CEO
will decide for himself.

25
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:23,420
Exactly.

26
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:40,970
Isn't that the liquor
you were saving?

27
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:44,140
If not on a day like today,
then when?

28
00:01:44,910 --> 00:01:46,010
Would you like a glass, Director?

29
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:47,980
I'm good.

30
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:51,420
By the way,

31
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:55,520
how did you find out about
Ko Eun Seol's criminal record?

32
00:01:56,650 --> 00:01:58,520
Her resume seemed suspicious.

33
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,660
So I asked some
of our old classmates,

34
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:02,460
and bingo.

35
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:03,960
I wasn't expecting
anything that big,

36
00:02:04,030 --> 00:02:06,000
but I got total goosebumps
when I heard about it.

37
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:08,000
It was absolutely thrilling.

38
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:11,000
From now on,
discuss things like that with me first.

39
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,540
Why? Were you that surprised?

40
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:18,810
You were lucky
it went your way this time,

41
00:02:19,510 --> 00:02:22,410
but in the future, don't be
so impulsive and blab like that.

42
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:24,050
Do you understand what I'm saying?

43
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:26,220
It went my way, so who cares?

44
00:02:26,350 --> 00:02:27,520
Why bother with a plan?

45
00:02:41,930 --> 00:02:42,930
Hey, Ms. Park.

46
00:02:43,470 --> 00:02:45,240
This is Ko Eun Seol.
Do you remember me?

47
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:47,270
Inmate 2751, Ko Eun Seol?

48
00:02:48,170 --> 00:02:49,910
Of course I remember you.

49
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:53,140
You made my time in prison
so much easier.

50
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:55,580
Anyway, what's up?

51
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,320
There's a favor I need to ask you.

52
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:04,560
A favor? Name it.
I'll do anything you ask.

53
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:06,930
So, what's the favor?

54
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:11,260
Can you put me in touch
with a business reporter?

55
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,230
I have something to report, sir.

56
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:18,470
What is it?

57
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:22,110
I was monitoring the lies spreading
about the contest online,

58
00:03:22,270 --> 00:03:23,780
and now articles are flooding in.

59
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:27,210
Really? What is this?

60
00:03:28,410 --> 00:03:30,420
"Discrimination
against ex-convicts,"

61
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:34,020
"outdated HR practices under fire?"

62
00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:38,060
Who on earth leaked this?

63
00:03:38,490 --> 00:03:40,890
Negative reports are out
from several securities firms,

64
00:03:40,990 --> 00:03:43,060
and the stock price
has dropped by 2.8 percent.

65
00:03:59,910 --> 00:04:01,550
Were you the one behind this?

66
00:04:03,110 --> 00:04:04,120
I'm not sure.

67
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:06,280
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

68
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:09,790
Wasn't it you
who leaked to the press?

69
00:04:10,990 --> 00:04:12,490
How could I do something like that?

70
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,630
I'm not that reckless.

71
00:04:16,630 --> 00:04:17,930
And most importantly,

72
00:04:19,030 --> 00:04:21,370
what power do I have, sir?

73
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,240
I see.

74
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:32,240
I've given it some thought,

75
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:35,350
and I think
it'd be meaningful to give...

76
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:38,880
a young person like you
a second chance.

77
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:42,420
You can start next week.

78
00:04:43,550 --> 00:04:44,560
Really?

79
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:47,630
Does that mean I'm officially hired?

80
00:04:49,030 --> 00:04:50,030
Yes.

81
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:53,770
Thank you. Thank you so much, sir.

82
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:56,600
You may go.

83
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,440
Right.

84
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:08,550
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

85
00:05:09,450 --> 00:05:11,020
Do you think Ko Eun Seol did it?

86
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:13,720
Of course.

87
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:19,120
There's nothing to worry about.

88
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:21,660
What can some
low-level designer accomplish...

89
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:23,590
just by getting into Cheongma?

90
00:05:24,330 --> 00:05:25,330
Right.

91
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:27,900
For now, let's focus on our work.

92
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:30,500
Look into the board members
of the scholarship foundation.

93
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:31,970
Everything
from their family relationships...

94
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,400
and medical records
to their personal tastes.

95
00:05:33,710 --> 00:05:34,940
Yes, ma'am.

96
00:05:49,050 --> 00:05:50,990
I just came from seeing the CEO.

97
00:05:51,990 --> 00:05:53,560
You're starting next week?

98
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,130
Yes.

99
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:00,000
It won't be easy.

100
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:03,530
Anyway, congratulations.

101
00:06:07,910 --> 00:06:09,570
Okay, then. I'll see you next week.

102
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:34,700
You think I'm going
to let this slide?

103
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,440
Mom,

104
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:49,680
it won't be long now.

105
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:52,920
I'll find the real killer...

106
00:06:53,890 --> 00:06:55,820
and make sure
they pay for their crime.

107
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:05,960
(Scholarship Foundation
Board Member Profiles)

108
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:08,730
(Battling liver cancer,
Recent reduction in activities)

109
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,140
Battling liver cancer?

110
00:07:24,250 --> 00:07:25,320
Hey, Eun Seol.

111
00:07:27,490 --> 00:07:28,490
What's up?

112
00:07:30,020 --> 00:07:31,020
Here, take this.

113
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:32,960
What is it?

114
00:07:35,130 --> 00:07:36,230
Congratulations on the new job.

115
00:07:37,130 --> 00:07:38,730
That wasn't cheap, you know.

116
00:07:41,770 --> 00:07:42,770
Thanks.

117
00:07:44,770 --> 00:07:47,410
You'll be late.
Hurry up and get ready for work.

118
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:10,860
I'm off, Mom.

119
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,400
All right.

120
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:53,800
This is Ko Eun Seol.
She's joining the team today.

121
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:54,870
Everyone, say hello.

122
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:58,480
Hello, I'm Ko Eun Seol.

123
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:00,110
I look forward to working
with you all.

124
00:09:00,850 --> 00:09:01,850
Ko Eun Seol?

125
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:04,720
You're the Ko Eun Seol
who won the grand prize?

126
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:06,480
Do you two know each other?

127
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:11,520
We went to high school together,
along with Hae Ra. I mean,

128
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:13,390
along with Ms. Kang.

129
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:15,430
Oh, I see.

130
00:09:15,990 --> 00:09:17,600
I'm Assistant Manager Lee Young Ung.

131
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:18,660
I hope we get along.

132
00:09:19,130 --> 00:09:21,130
Yes, I look forward
to working with you.

133
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,500
Team Leader Kang,
aren't you going to say hello?

134
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:25,740
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

135
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:29,940
Team Leader Kang.

136
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,410
I'm Kang Hae Ra,
head of the Design Team.

137
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:36,910
Satisfied?

138
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:42,520
All right. Mr. Lee, Ms. Kim,

139
00:09:42,590 --> 00:09:44,690
please help Ms. Ko get up to speed.

140
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:47,360
Good luck, then.

141
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:48,630
Thanks.

142
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:57,540
You can use that desk.

143
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:06,180
Okay, so the first thing
you should do is...

144
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:08,880
Ms. Kang.

145
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:10,820
What should I have
Eun Seol do first?

146
00:10:11,450 --> 00:10:12,580
Ji Soo,

147
00:10:12,850 --> 00:10:14,490
do you still think
we're in high school?

148
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,120
I'm sorry.

149
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:19,990
What task should I assign to Ms. Ko?

150
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:26,860
Ms. Ko,

151
00:10:27,030 --> 00:10:29,200
I'm analyzing the trends
for the first half of the year,

152
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:30,300
so how about lending me a hand?

153
00:10:30,370 --> 00:10:31,370
Assistant Manager Lee!

154
00:10:33,470 --> 00:10:35,470
Why are you pawning your work off
on someone else?

155
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:38,810
You don't want to work?
Then resign and get out.

156
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:41,480
No, that's not it. I'm sorry.

157
00:10:45,250 --> 00:10:46,380
Then, Ms. Kang,

158
00:10:47,150 --> 00:10:49,190
what is it that I should be doing?

159
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:31,530
Are you crazy?
What the heck is this?

160
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,770
Officially, it was a mistake.

161
00:11:35,270 --> 00:11:37,800
Unofficially, it's payback
for what you did.

162
00:11:40,540 --> 00:11:41,540
Hey.

163
00:11:41,970 --> 00:11:43,840
What exactly did I do?

164
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:46,740
Didn't you spread rumors
in the financial district,

165
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:48,010
causing Cheongma's stock to tank?

166
00:11:49,210 --> 00:11:50,210
Beats me.

167
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:52,420
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

168
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:55,550
You're unbelievable, Ko Eun Seol.

169
00:11:55,990 --> 00:11:58,590
Why would you go to such lengths
just to get into Cheongma?

170
00:12:02,230 --> 00:12:05,630
Don't tell me
you're still interested in Seok Jin.

171
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:09,500
And what if I am?

172
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:12,340
What?

173
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:17,070
Stop harassing me
and put me to work,

174
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:18,140
Ms. Kang.

175
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,710
Put someone like you to work?

176
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:23,250
Just stay out of the way.

177
00:12:28,890 --> 00:12:30,190
Listen up, everyone.

178
00:12:30,690 --> 00:12:33,520
Ko Eun Seol will be leaving soon,
so act like she's not here.

179
00:12:33,690 --> 00:12:35,630
If I catch any of you
talking to her...

180
00:12:35,730 --> 00:12:38,200
Well, you know what'll happen.

181
00:12:39,160 --> 00:12:40,160
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

182
00:12:45,970 --> 00:12:49,010
Did Ms. Kang and Ko Eun Seol
not get along in high school?

183
00:12:50,310 --> 00:12:51,440
That's an understatement.

184
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:55,650
Ko Eun Seol is really in for it.

185
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:59,950
But she's no pushover,

186
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:01,150
so it'll be interesting to watch.

187
00:13:05,460 --> 00:13:08,030
Ms. Kang spilled coffee on me,

188
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:09,960
so I have to go change my clothes.

189
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:11,930
I'll be right back.

190
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:26,010
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

191
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:27,850
Did Ko Eun Seol come in today?

192
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:29,380
Yes.

193
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:33,050
What's the market sentiment?

194
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:35,850
Since we issued a correction
and responded proactively,

195
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,560
it seems the whole thing
is blowing over.

196
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:39,720
You don't need to worry.

197
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:40,720
Good.

198
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:44,730
What do you think, Chief Cha?

199
00:13:45,430 --> 00:13:46,760
What are you referring to, sir?

200
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:50,070
She spreads fake news
to get what she wants...

201
00:13:50,130 --> 00:13:51,870
and goes after it ruthlessly.

202
00:13:52,270 --> 00:13:54,340
Is that really someone
we should hire?

203
00:13:54,710 --> 00:13:56,370
Are you referring to Ko Eun Seol?

204
00:13:58,480 --> 00:13:59,740
That can't be right.

205
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:04,620
She's not the type of person
to lie to others for her own gain...

206
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:06,250
or cause them harm.

207
00:14:06,450 --> 00:14:07,450
Really?

208
00:14:07,450 --> 00:14:08,950
How would you know that?

209
00:14:09,650 --> 00:14:10,650
Oh, right.

210
00:14:11,290 --> 00:14:13,060
Since Ko Eun Seol
was Hae Ra's classmate,

211
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,430
I suppose you'd know her.

212
00:14:15,290 --> 00:14:16,790
Were you two close in school?

213
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:19,960
I know enough about
the kind of person she is.

214
00:14:20,730 --> 00:14:21,730
I see.

215
00:14:22,270 --> 00:14:24,470
Perhaps she's changed.

216
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,000
After ten years in prison,

217
00:14:27,370 --> 00:14:30,470
I wouldn't be surprised
if her very nature has changed.

218
00:14:34,910 --> 00:14:36,150
In any case,

219
00:14:36,410 --> 00:14:38,320
make sure the people
at that awards ceremony...

220
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:39,720
keep their mouths shut.

221
00:14:40,550 --> 00:14:43,050
I don't want any more trouble
over this.

222
00:14:43,350 --> 00:14:45,490
I've already had them sign
non-disclosure agreements.

223
00:14:46,490 --> 00:14:47,490
Well, then.

224
00:14:48,790 --> 00:14:49,790
Chief Cha.

225
00:14:50,660 --> 00:14:51,660
Yes?

226
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,600
What are your plans with my Hae Ra?

227
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:58,770
You're not actually thinking
of marrying her, are you?

228
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:06,340
With your blessing, sir,
I plan to marry her.

229
00:15:09,350 --> 00:15:10,780
And if I don't give you
my permission?

230
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:14,050
Then I'll wait until you do.

231
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:17,050
Do you love her?

232
00:15:21,290 --> 00:15:22,890
You can't answer.

233
00:15:23,890 --> 00:15:25,930
And yet you want to marry her?

234
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:27,360
Marriage...

235
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:31,440
I think there's more to it
than just love.

236
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:33,900
However, I do care for Hae Ra.

237
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:35,910
Perhaps not as much
as she cares for me.

238
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:37,780
And...

239
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:41,980
I also believe there is no one
more suited to be Hae Ra's husband.

240
00:15:43,810 --> 00:15:46,480
Is that honesty or arrogance?

241
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:50,890
It doesn't matter which it is.

242
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:53,860
I have no intention
of letting you two get married.

243
00:15:58,530 --> 00:15:59,660
You're dismissed.

244
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:01,900
Yes, sir.

245
00:16:09,170 --> 00:16:10,540
Unbelievable.

246
00:16:17,050 --> 00:16:18,520
You called for me, Ms. Joo?

247
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,650
It's about Director Han Cheol Soo.

248
00:16:20,950 --> 00:16:23,050
He went to college
with CEO Kang, right?

249
00:16:23,490 --> 00:16:26,660
Yes. He was appointed director
on CEO Kang's recommendation.

250
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,730
According to the file you gave me,

251
00:16:28,790 --> 00:16:30,990
it says he's battling liver cancer.

252
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:33,360
How serious is it?

253
00:16:33,830 --> 00:16:36,570
It's terminal. I heard he has
less than a year left.

254
00:16:36,670 --> 00:16:37,770
Is that right?

255
00:16:37,970 --> 00:16:40,640
Then we'll need
a replacement director soon.

256
00:16:42,170 --> 00:16:44,040
Do you have something else planned?

257
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:46,310
Find someone
in the Chairman's circle...

258
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:48,310
who loves money and prestige.

259
00:16:48,580 --> 00:16:49,710
Yes, ma'am.

260
00:16:49,950 --> 00:16:53,080
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

261
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:16,810
Hello.

262
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:19,380
I'm Ko Eun Seol,
new to the design team.

263
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:21,610
I see. How can I help you?

264
00:17:22,150 --> 00:17:24,250
I just have a quick question.

265
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:27,850
Here, this is for you.

266
00:17:29,190 --> 00:17:30,920
You didn't have to do that.

267
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:33,720
Still, thanks.

268
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:36,560
So, what did you want to ask?

269
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:40,360
I need to request a company car
for a client meeting next week,

270
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:42,200
but I'm not sure
what the process is.

271
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:44,230
Just get
your team leader's approval...

272
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:45,570
and then file the request.

273
00:17:46,270 --> 00:17:47,270
Really?

274
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:50,470
Then, can I be assigned
any car that I want?

275
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:54,580
Well, no. What kind of car you get
depends on your rank.

276
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:57,110
- It depends on my rank?
- Yes.

277
00:17:57,110 --> 00:17:58,850
Since you're a new hire,

278
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:00,820
you'll be assigned a compact car.

279
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:02,750
I see.

280
00:18:03,850 --> 00:18:08,330
Then what rank do I need to reach
to get a full-size sedan?

281
00:18:08,490 --> 00:18:09,490
A department head.

282
00:18:10,530 --> 00:18:11,630
Department head?

283
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:13,200
Yes.

284
00:18:14,900 --> 00:18:17,000
But, why do you ask?

285
00:18:18,040 --> 00:18:19,840
Oh, I was just curious...

286
00:18:20,670 --> 00:18:21,940
Actually, I'm just envious.

287
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:24,340
See you next time, then.

288
00:18:27,410 --> 00:18:29,910
She left ages ago.
Why isn't she back yet?

289
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:37,790
What do you think you're doing,
slacking off on your first day?

290
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:41,560
I had nothing to do,
so I took a tour of the building.

291
00:18:42,030 --> 00:18:43,490
What? You took a tour?

292
00:18:44,330 --> 00:18:45,330
Yes.

293
00:18:48,670 --> 00:18:52,140
Assistant Manager Lee, Ji Soo,
let's grab lunch. My treat.

294
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:54,770
Really? What are you treating us to?

295
00:18:54,770 --> 00:18:56,170
Anything you want.

296
00:18:56,670 --> 00:18:57,670
Then how about steak?

297
00:19:00,310 --> 00:19:02,150
Enjoy your lunch, Eun Seol.

298
00:19:02,410 --> 00:19:03,980
Yes, you too.

299
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:19,700
(Employee Search)

300
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:26,470
Where did everyone go?

301
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,940
Oh, they all went to lunch.

302
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:31,980
Why didn't you go with them?

303
00:19:32,510 --> 00:19:34,410
I wasn't really hungry.

304
00:19:35,850 --> 00:19:38,050
Anyway, what brings you here?

305
00:19:38,050 --> 00:19:41,290
Since it's your first day, I thought
I'd treat everyone to lunch.

306
00:19:41,650 --> 00:19:42,920
Looks like I was a step too late.

307
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:47,520
You should still eat,
even if you don't have an appetite.

308
00:19:47,930 --> 00:19:49,560
Want to go grab something with me?

309
00:19:50,260 --> 00:19:53,960
No. It's okay.
I'm really not hungry.

310
00:19:55,430 --> 00:19:56,470
All right, then.

311
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:59,400
Oh, right.

312
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:06,240
The CEO suspects that you're the one
who leaked the story.

313
00:20:06,980 --> 00:20:07,980
That's not true, is it?

314
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:12,480
Why aren't you answering?

315
00:20:13,650 --> 00:20:14,850
Don't tell me you did it.

316
00:20:16,050 --> 00:20:17,050
No,

317
00:20:17,490 --> 00:20:19,320
I'd never do something like that.

318
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:20,860
Exactly.

319
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:23,060
You're not that kind of person.

320
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:26,630
Well, keep up the good work.

321
00:20:41,610 --> 00:20:43,510
Teun Teun,
let's have some watermelon.

322
00:20:43,850 --> 00:20:45,150
Okay, Mom.

323
00:20:46,850 --> 00:20:47,920
Here you go.

324
00:20:48,490 --> 00:20:51,720
Gosh, it's so hot.
I feel like I'm boiling alive.

325
00:20:51,860 --> 00:20:54,060
It's too hot.

326
00:20:55,030 --> 00:20:58,130
Mom, what's that sound?

327
00:20:59,930 --> 00:21:01,060
I don't know.

328
00:21:02,330 --> 00:21:04,030
- Dig in.
- Okay.

329
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:10,440
Gosh, it's hot. I'm boiling alive.
It's too hot.

330
00:21:11,170 --> 00:21:15,450
My goodness, it's so hot.
Gosh, it's hot.

331
00:21:20,050 --> 00:21:23,050
Ma'am, what are you doing out here?

332
00:21:23,050 --> 00:21:24,350
What do you think?

333
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:25,790
My room's like a sauna,

334
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:28,030
so I came out here
to catch a breeze.

335
00:21:28,190 --> 00:21:30,560
- Gosh, it's hot.
- What breeze? Goodness.

336
00:21:31,230 --> 00:21:32,930
The sun is scorching out here.

337
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:35,300
Ma'am,
you're going to get heatstroke.

338
00:21:35,330 --> 00:21:37,700
What's the worst that can happen?
Me dying?

339
00:21:39,140 --> 00:21:42,240
Why? Are you worried you'll have
to deal with a dead body?

340
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,940
Then let me come in
and share the AC with you.

341
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:51,210
Why don't you come inside
for a bit then?

342
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:53,720
You should've said so sooner.

343
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:56,990
My, it's hot.

344
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:04,800
It's so cool in here.

345
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:09,300
Oh, my, that watermelon
looks delicious.

346
00:22:10,330 --> 00:22:11,740
Have some, ma'am.

347
00:22:12,470 --> 00:22:14,500
You're such a sweet boy.

348
00:22:15,270 --> 00:22:18,940
You need to keep respecting
your elders like this, okay?

349
00:22:19,010 --> 00:22:20,010
Yes, ma'am.

350
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:24,310
By the way,
doesn't your dad live with you?

351
00:22:24,310 --> 00:22:25,980
I don't think I've seen him around.

352
00:22:26,120 --> 00:22:27,580
I don't have a dad.

353
00:22:30,220 --> 00:22:32,660
You don't have a dad?

354
00:22:33,460 --> 00:22:34,460
That's right.

355
00:22:35,490 --> 00:22:36,490
Are you divorced?

356
00:22:37,190 --> 00:22:40,730
Ma'am, can't you just enjoy the AC
and be on your way?

357
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:45,700
Come on, that's not very neighborly.
You can tell me all about it.

358
00:22:45,970 --> 00:22:47,370
Why did you get a divorce?

359
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:49,940
I'm not divorced.

360
00:22:50,270 --> 00:22:51,980
If you're not divorced...

361
00:22:53,510 --> 00:22:55,080
Are you a widow?

362
00:22:55,410 --> 00:22:57,150
Or was the father
never in the picture?

363
00:22:59,120 --> 00:23:00,120
Ma'am,

364
00:23:00,780 --> 00:23:03,320
if you keep invading
my privacy like this,

365
00:23:03,390 --> 00:23:05,760
you won't be able to share our AC.

366
00:23:06,290 --> 00:23:08,830
Look who's bragging
over a little air conditioning.

367
00:23:12,830 --> 00:23:15,070
This watermelon is so sweet.
Goodness.

368
00:23:18,140 --> 00:23:19,300
It's so sweet.

369
00:23:20,340 --> 00:23:21,840
She's so petty.

370
00:23:21,910 --> 00:23:24,470
We'll get our own AC, okay?

371
00:23:26,180 --> 00:23:27,980
Grandma, why are you coming
out of there again?

372
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:31,950
Were you begging
to share their AC again?

373
00:23:32,020 --> 00:23:33,780
Am I a beggar? Why would I beg?

374
00:23:34,020 --> 00:23:36,450
You said she was stingy.
Why do you keep going back?

375
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:37,890
It's not like they welcome you.

376
00:23:38,120 --> 00:23:40,460
Whether they welcome me or not
is their business.

377
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,990
What am I supposed to do
when I'm about to boil to death?

378
00:23:43,490 --> 00:23:44,760
Gosh, it's so hot.

379
00:23:46,930 --> 00:23:49,430
That lady can probably
survive anything.

380
00:23:50,270 --> 00:23:51,270
Excuse me.

381
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,410
Can I talk to you for a minute?

382
00:23:56,310 --> 00:23:57,310
About what?

383
00:23:58,410 --> 00:24:00,340
Please do something
about your grandmother.

384
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:04,920
At this rate, she's going to spend
the entire summer at my house.

385
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:06,980
I looked into getting an AC,

386
00:24:06,980 --> 00:24:09,150
but they're completely booked up
for the rest of the year.

387
00:24:10,450 --> 00:24:11,490
So?

388
00:24:12,390 --> 00:24:13,390
That's just the situation.

389
00:24:14,860 --> 00:24:19,130
So you're not going to do anything
about her coming over?

390
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:21,260
It's not like I'm forcing her to go.

391
00:24:21,700 --> 00:24:22,730
What?

392
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:24,800
Then...

393
00:24:27,870 --> 00:24:30,240
I can't believe
how shameless they are!

394
00:24:32,380 --> 00:24:34,710
I'm so furious. Darn it.

395
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:38,880
Ms. Kang, aren't you heading home?

396
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:41,380
I will soon. You all go ahead.

397
00:24:41,890 --> 00:24:43,520
See you tomorrow then.

398
00:24:54,030 --> 00:24:56,930
In that case,
I'll be heading out too.

399
00:24:57,300 --> 00:24:58,770
How long are you planning
to stick it out?

400
00:25:03,970 --> 00:25:05,380
It's after hours,

401
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,710
so I can drop
the formalities, right?

402
00:25:08,680 --> 00:25:09,710
Hey.

403
00:25:10,280 --> 00:25:14,050
It's useless no matter what you try.

404
00:25:14,320 --> 00:25:16,420
You know where I've been.

405
00:25:18,290 --> 00:25:19,820
I even survived in there.

406
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:22,730
Do you really think
this will make me quit?

407
00:25:24,390 --> 00:25:26,560
You're more naive than you look.

408
00:25:28,030 --> 00:25:29,830
Hey, say that again.

409
00:25:34,070 --> 00:25:35,770
All I'm saying is that...

410
00:25:36,710 --> 00:25:39,040
you should pick your fights
more carefully.

411
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:41,280
Then...

412
00:25:42,150 --> 00:25:44,050
I'll see you tomorrow, Ms. Kang.

413
00:25:46,980 --> 00:25:48,180
Has she lost her darn mind?

414
00:25:49,220 --> 00:25:50,220
Unbelievable!

415
00:25:54,060 --> 00:25:55,160
How's this tea?

416
00:25:56,060 --> 00:25:58,160
It's nice. Why?

417
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:02,070
This is a special tea sent by
a Cheongma scholarship student...

418
00:26:02,070 --> 00:26:03,770
to say thank you.

419
00:26:04,670 --> 00:26:05,670
Is that right?

420
00:26:06,640 --> 00:26:09,170
It's nice of them to express
their gratitude like this.

421
00:26:09,570 --> 00:26:10,870
Tell me about it.

422
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:13,380
That's why I'm thinking
of increasing...

423
00:26:13,440 --> 00:26:14,910
the scholarship budget next year.

424
00:26:15,210 --> 00:26:17,210
What? By how much?

425
00:26:17,450 --> 00:26:19,220
About 30 percent?

426
00:26:19,420 --> 00:26:21,690
Honey, no, we can't do that.

427
00:26:22,690 --> 00:26:25,560
What? Why not?

428
00:26:25,860 --> 00:26:28,490
Honey, it's already enough.

429
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:32,660
With raw material costs soaring,
we have so many other expenses.

430
00:26:32,860 --> 00:26:35,230
And you want to increase
the scholarship budget?

431
00:26:35,400 --> 00:26:36,830
We should be cutting it,
if anything.

432
00:26:37,530 --> 00:26:39,800
Don't you know the company
has to do well first...

433
00:26:40,500 --> 00:26:42,070
for the foundation to be maintained?

434
00:26:43,610 --> 00:26:44,940
That's true, but...

435
00:26:46,780 --> 00:26:47,780
All right.

436
00:26:49,780 --> 00:26:52,920
Gosh, you're too idealistic
for your own good.

437
00:26:53,080 --> 00:26:55,620
Do you think running a business
is that easy?

438
00:26:57,890 --> 00:26:59,390
I said I get it.

439
00:27:02,490 --> 00:27:03,490
What...

440
00:27:11,230 --> 00:27:13,670
I think the Chairman
is a little upset.

441
00:27:14,670 --> 00:27:17,370
I'll just have
to make it up to her tomorrow.

442
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:36,160
Let's see.

443
00:27:36,230 --> 00:27:38,060
(June 5: 12 suspects
with access to company cars)

444
00:27:38,700 --> 00:27:39,700
What's this?

445
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:43,130
This lists everyone who had access
to the company car...

446
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:45,200
used to meet Lee Jung Tae on June 5.

447
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:48,340
Are you saying that
one of the people here...

448
00:27:48,710 --> 00:27:50,270
is the culprit we're looking for?

449
00:27:50,810 --> 00:27:51,810
Yes.

450
00:27:52,310 --> 00:27:53,640
How did you figure this out?

451
00:27:54,010 --> 00:27:55,510
According to General Affairs,

452
00:27:55,510 --> 00:27:58,050
those cars are only assigned
to department heads.

453
00:28:00,080 --> 00:28:02,820
So after excluding people
dispatched overseas or on leave,

454
00:28:02,890 --> 00:28:04,950
I narrowed it down
to department heads at HQ.

455
00:28:06,020 --> 00:28:07,290
I see.

456
00:28:09,360 --> 00:28:10,830
Eun Seol, this is incredible.

457
00:28:11,290 --> 00:28:13,430
How did you find all this out
in one day?

458
00:28:16,170 --> 00:28:20,200
Then we should start by looking into
what they were doing on June 5.

459
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:22,070
We'll do that together.

460
00:28:22,870 --> 00:28:23,910
I'll do it by myself.

461
00:28:25,010 --> 00:28:26,010
Why?

462
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:29,150
I can't put you in danger too,
Attorney Seo.

463
00:28:30,550 --> 00:28:31,610
Eun Seol, come on.

464
00:28:33,080 --> 00:28:34,980
If anything happens to me,

465
00:28:35,620 --> 00:28:37,850
we'll still need you at Cheongma.

466
00:28:38,790 --> 00:28:39,790
Don't you agree?

467
00:28:41,590 --> 00:28:44,590
Then promise me you'll reach out
if you need help.

468
00:28:45,630 --> 00:28:46,630
Of course.

469
00:28:53,040 --> 00:28:55,570
(Cheongma)

470
00:28:59,580 --> 00:29:00,580
What's this?

471
00:29:00,910 --> 00:29:02,250
It's five years' worth...

472
00:29:02,310 --> 00:29:04,410
of competitor product review data
and market research reports.

473
00:29:06,250 --> 00:29:07,320
And?

474
00:29:07,850 --> 00:29:11,790
Sort all this by brand, material,
price range, and sales trends,

475
00:29:11,790 --> 00:29:12,920
and compile everything
into a database.

476
00:29:14,260 --> 00:29:15,690
Sure. Understood.

477
00:29:16,130 --> 00:29:18,560
I need it next week, so finish it
by the end of this week.

478
00:29:20,530 --> 00:29:23,070
Wait, all of this by this week?

479
00:29:23,370 --> 00:29:25,240
What's wrong? Can't you do it?

480
00:29:25,940 --> 00:29:27,270
If you can't, then leave.

481
00:29:30,240 --> 00:29:32,380
No. I'll get it done.

482
00:29:33,280 --> 00:29:34,380
You should've said so
in the first place.

483
00:29:43,290 --> 00:29:46,390
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

484
00:29:46,460 --> 00:29:47,460
Honey.

485
00:29:48,960 --> 00:29:50,030
Let's go to lunch.

486
00:29:52,060 --> 00:29:53,430
Go by yourself.

487
00:29:55,170 --> 00:29:57,830
Are you pouting
because of what I said yesterday?

488
00:30:00,800 --> 00:30:02,840
Come on, don't pout
over something like that.

489
00:30:02,840 --> 00:30:04,340
It's not like you.

490
00:30:06,210 --> 00:30:07,980
Saying it once would've been enough.

491
00:30:08,310 --> 00:30:11,180
Did you have to embarrass me
like that in front of Director Joo?

492
00:30:11,580 --> 00:30:13,780
What? Embarrass you?

493
00:30:15,520 --> 00:30:18,150
Well, you shouldn't have said
something so childish.

494
00:30:18,990 --> 00:30:19,990
Honey.

495
00:30:21,120 --> 00:30:22,130
Forget it.

496
00:30:22,430 --> 00:30:23,830
You need to focus less
on other things...

497
00:30:23,890 --> 00:30:26,530
and start looking
for potential suitors for Hae Ra.

498
00:30:26,630 --> 00:30:29,070
It's time to let go of Seok Jin.

499
00:30:29,970 --> 00:30:32,040
Why? Did something happen
with Seok Jin?

500
00:30:32,700 --> 00:30:34,070
What a joke.

501
00:30:34,800 --> 00:30:37,770
He said he'd marry her
if I gave my permission,

502
00:30:37,970 --> 00:30:39,840
so I asked him if he loves Hae Ra.

503
00:30:39,840 --> 00:30:41,680
He couldn't answer me.

504
00:30:42,110 --> 00:30:43,880
What? Really?

505
00:30:44,350 --> 00:30:45,350
Yes.

506
00:30:45,580 --> 00:30:47,850
He's just trying to marry her
for her background.

507
00:30:48,150 --> 00:30:49,420
That shameless jerk.

508
00:30:50,050 --> 00:30:52,560
Come on, I doubt that.

509
00:30:54,360 --> 00:30:56,960
You're also searching for a suitor
from a good family,

510
00:30:57,590 --> 00:30:59,430
so why blame Seok Jin?

511
00:31:00,430 --> 00:31:01,430
What?

512
00:31:02,030 --> 00:31:03,130
Am I wrong?

513
00:31:03,470 --> 00:31:07,070
How is that the same?
You're unbelievable.

514
00:31:08,270 --> 00:31:10,510
You're buying lunch, right?

515
00:31:11,570 --> 00:31:13,540
Of course. Now, let's go.

516
00:31:13,980 --> 00:31:15,210
- Come on.
- Unbelievable.

517
00:31:15,780 --> 00:31:18,150
- I'll let it go this time.
- Let's go.

518
00:31:19,620 --> 00:31:21,420
All right. Shall we?

519
00:31:21,820 --> 00:31:23,450
Ms. Kang, aren't you going to lunch?

520
00:31:24,590 --> 00:31:25,590
I am.

521
00:31:27,520 --> 00:31:29,060
What should we eat today?

522
00:31:30,730 --> 00:31:32,060
How about that new taco place?

523
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:34,500
Tacos? Sure, sounds good.

524
00:31:42,140 --> 00:31:43,670
Eun Seol, aren't you having lunch?

525
00:31:45,010 --> 00:31:46,010
You all go ahead.

526
00:31:46,980 --> 00:31:47,980
Okay, then.

527
00:31:58,590 --> 00:32:01,860
(Sales Operations Team)

528
00:32:17,710 --> 00:32:19,510
(September, August, July, June, May)

529
00:32:19,580 --> 00:32:20,580
June...

530
00:32:22,780 --> 00:32:24,280
(June 4-8: Shanghai business trip,
11: Trip report)

531
00:32:29,550 --> 00:32:30,550
Hold on.

532
00:32:32,490 --> 00:32:35,330
How did you and Ko Eun Seol
first meet?

533
00:32:37,760 --> 00:32:40,360
I was Eun Seol's defense lawyer
when she was framed.

534
00:32:40,460 --> 00:32:41,500
I see.

535
00:32:42,370 --> 00:32:45,370
Then can you tell me
what happened back then?

536
00:32:46,240 --> 00:32:47,240
What about it?

537
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:50,770
I'm curious about the circumstances
of her mother's death,

538
00:32:51,110 --> 00:32:53,180
and how Eun Seol was framed.

539
00:32:53,810 --> 00:32:55,010
Why are you curious about that?

540
00:32:57,210 --> 00:32:59,650
Oh, right. You were
her senior in high school.

541
00:33:02,220 --> 00:33:03,890
Please, tell me. I'm asking you.

542
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:07,890
No, I'm afraid I can't do that.

543
00:33:08,790 --> 00:33:11,290
As her lawyer, I'm bound
by attorney-client privilege.

544
00:33:11,590 --> 00:33:13,730
- Well, then.
- By any chance,

545
00:33:15,030 --> 00:33:17,900
was Eun Seol the one
who leaked the story about her?

546
00:33:19,600 --> 00:33:20,600
No.

547
00:33:21,570 --> 00:33:22,570
No?

548
00:33:23,510 --> 00:33:25,740
That's right. Eun Seol didn't do it.

549
00:33:26,210 --> 00:33:27,210
How do you know that?

550
00:33:28,610 --> 00:33:30,080
How do you know that it wasn't her?

551
00:33:58,270 --> 00:34:01,940
(A Trap Called Desire)

552
00:34:02,110 --> 00:34:05,450
You should start thinking
about a replacement director.

553
00:34:05,580 --> 00:34:08,750
I knew I could count on you
to look out for me, Director Joo.

554
00:34:08,790 --> 00:34:10,790
I'm going to take
Seok Jin away from you.

555
00:34:11,020 --> 00:34:12,360
Let's get along.

556
00:34:12,360 --> 00:34:14,220
If you can't, at least fake it.

557
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:15,430
What is it that you want?

558
00:34:15,630 --> 00:34:16,630
A kiss.

559
00:34:16,660 --> 00:34:20,130
I'm warning you.
Stop hanging out with Eun Seol.

560
00:34:20,200 --> 00:34:22,000
There's something
I absolutely need to confirm,

561
00:34:22,030 --> 00:34:23,230
Could you please show it to me?

562
00:34:23,230 --> 00:34:25,840
You two don't seem like
just friends from school.

563
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:28,200
I hope you don't do anything
to disappoint me.

564
00:34:28,200 --> 00:34:29,340
You're hiding something, aren't you?

565
00:34:29,340 --> 00:34:32,380
Eun Seol, you're nothing like
the Ko Eun Seol I remember.

566
00:34:33,110 --> 00:34:35,110
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
